+## Open a file in the window
+
+Use the desktop executable `camcraft-ui` to open one file from the
+command line. This starts the window; `camcraft-cli` remains the headless
+tool described below.
+
+```sh
+camcraft-ui part.step
+camcraft-ui job.camproj
+camcraft-ui --mcp-port 7915 part.stl
+```
+
+The window accepts `.stl`, `.obj`, `.step`, `.stp`, native `.sc`
+Solidcraft designs, and `.camproj` projects. A model goes through the
+normal import command; a project goes through the normal open command.
+An option's value is not treated as a file path.
+
+More than one file, an unknown extension or a path that is not a file is
+refused by name on the status line (`open refused: ...`). The window
+still starts with an empty project. This does not forward files to an
+already running window. On macOS, passing the path to the binary works;
+`open -a` file events are not supported by this startup argument path.
